{"id": "85883", "name": "נגזרת של 1/x^(1/n)+c (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Differentiate {{CT:0}} with respect to {{CT:1}}.</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\"> [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Split the sum by linearity, write the root as a power with a negative exponent, and apply the power rule.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — Linearity</b><br>Recall:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\frac{d}{d{{CT:2}}}\\left(\\frac{1}{{{CT:2}}^{\\frac{1}{{CT:3}}}}+{{CT:4}}\\right)=\\frac{d}{d{{CT:2}}}\\left(\\frac{1}{{{CT:2}}^{\\frac{1}{{CT:3}}}}\\right)+\\frac{d}{d{{CT:2}}}\\left({{CT:4}}\\right). \\]</p>Now remember that the differential of a constant is \\(0\\). So we need to find:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\frac{d}{d{{CT:2}}}\\left(\\frac{1}{{{CT:2}}^{\\frac{1}{{CT:3}}}}\\right). \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — Laws of indices</b><br>Using the laws of indices this is:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\frac{d}{d{{CT:2}}}\\left({{CT:2}}^{-\\frac{1}{{CT:3}}}\\right). \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 3 — The power rule</b><br>We can now apply the standard rules of differentiation to get:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\frac{d}{d{{CT:2}}}\\left({{CT:2}}^{-\\frac{1}{{CT:3}}}\\right)=-\\frac{1}{{CT:3}}{{CT:2}}^{{CT:5}}=-\\frac{1}{{{CT:3}}\\cdot{{CT:2}}^{{CT:6}}}. \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<span class='correct'>Correct answer, well done.</span>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<span class='partially'>Your answer is partially correct.</span>", "prtincorrect": "<span class='incorrect'>Incorrect answer.</span>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "Diff", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "diff(p,v)", "testoptions": "v", "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "DIF-EXP-TRUE", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "DIF-EXP-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["c", "n", "p", "q", "r", "v"], "nvariants": 50}